{"type":"text","timestamp":1793119717976,"sessionID":"ses_e81bca6efffenyBU8uZOWNJ8yL","part":{"id":"prt_17e438529001IHsRQOY2jDSuDu","sessionID":"ses_e81bca6efffenyBU8uZOWNJ8yL","messageID":"msg_17e436eb6001i139YUj6r6d9zW","type":"text","text":"CHANGE: Clarify that the transition loss is an auxiliary training term: it does not change source-to-codeword assignment or successor reconstruction, which remains tied to the successor’s own residual and assigned codeword. The objection identifies a possible pressure from the auxiliary term, but not a collapse implied by the mechanism; collapse would require that term to override identity-preserving reconstruction. | why the objection no longer applies\nUNCHANGED: The source codeword is selected to minimize distance to its source residual, and the transition loss encourages that codeword to be closer to the successor residual.\nREMAINING: Without a specified bound on the transition loss relative to reconstruction, I accept that it could exert enough pressure to harm successor identity preservation.","time":{"start":1793119716649,"end":1793119717976}}}
